# Blynk IoT Health Monitoring

## Description

Blynk IoT Health Monitoring is an Internet of Things (IoT)-based health monitoring system developed using Arduino and the Blynk platform. It enables real-time monitoring of health sensor data by sending information to the Blynk Cloud, allowing users to access their health data anytime and anywhere through a smartphone.

This project was created as a learning project to explore IoT, Arduino programming, wireless communication, cloud connectivity, and real-time health monitoring.

## Features

- Real-time health monitoring
- Live sensor data visualization on the Blynk app
- Wi-Fi connectivity using ESP8266/ESP32
- User-friendly mobile dashboard
- Automatic data updates
- Cloud-based remote monitoring

## Hardware Components

- Arduino Uno / ESP8266 / ESP32
- Health sensor(s) (depending on the project)
- ESP8266 Wi-Fi Module (if using Arduino Uno)
- Smartphone with the Blynk IoT app
- USB cable
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires
- Power supply

## Software Requirements

- Arduino IDE
- Blynk IoT Platform
- Required Arduino libraries
- Blynk Mobile Application

## How It Works

1. The health sensor collects physiological data.
2. The microcontroller processes the sensor readings.
3. The processed data is transmitted via Wi-Fi to the Blynk Cloud.
4. The Blynk mobile application receives and displays the data in real time.
5. Users can monitor the device remotely as long as it is connected to the internet.

