## Installation

1. Clone this repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/Blynk-IoT-Health-Monitoring.git
```

2. Open the project in **Arduino IDE**.

3. Install all required libraries.

4. Configure the following credentials:

- Blynk Template ID
- Device Name
- Auth Token
- Wi-Fi SSID
- Wi-Fi Password

5. Upload the program to your Arduino or ESP board.

6. Open the **Blynk IoT** mobile application.

7. The device will automatically connect and begin sending sensor data to your dashboard.

## Results

The system successfully transmits health sensor data to the Blynk IoT platform in real time through an internet connection. Users can monitor sensor readings remotely using the Blynk mobile application.

## Future Improvements

- Push notifications for abnormal health conditions
- Cloud database integration
- Historical data visualization
- Support for additional health sensors
- Web dashboard integration
- Data logging and analytics

